# Server & Slurm Rules (READ BEFORE RUNNING ANYTHING HEAVY)

This project runs on a shared university Slurm cluster. See `docs/SERVER_RUNBOOK.md`
and `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md`. Violating these can crash the login node for everyone.

## Golden rule: never compute on the login node

- The login node is for editing, `git`, file inspection, and submitting jobs ONLY.
- NEVER run training, full-dataset preprocessing, or any GPU/heavy-CPU job on the
  login node. Submit via `sbatch`, or use `srun`/`salloc` for an interactive session.
- Quick, cheap, < ~30 s sanity checks (versions, reading one file header, listing
  dirs, building the manifest) are acceptable on the login node.
- A SINGLE-session preprocessing smoke test runs via `srun`, not on the login node.

## Cluster facts (verified — official doc http://10.26.1.75:58080/, see docs/SERVER_RUNBOOK.md)

- Topology: `login01` (10.26.1.75, submit/monitor only) + GPU nodes `gpu01-05` (8× NVIDIA 4090D
  each, no SSH — Slurm only) + `storge` (10.26.1.74, file/IO node, no Slurm/compute). One shared
  NFS `/share`.
- Partitions: `gpu2node` (default = gpu01,02) and `gpu3node` (gpu03,04,05). TIMELIMIT effectively
  unlimited -> ALWAYS set `-t`.
- GPU conda env: **`mi_torch_cu118`** (torch 2.7.1+cu118, CUDA works) — use for all GPU jobs. The
  old `mi_torch` is CPU-only — do NOT use it for GPU. Activate base:
  `/share/software/anaconda3/2024.10/etc/profile.d/conda.sh`. Modules via `module load` (e.g.
  `cuda/11.8` or `cuda/12.6`).
- Monitoring (on login01): `slmwatch` (cluster + your quota/jobs), `gpuwatch` (per-GPU usage),
  `user-tools` (list helpers); plus `sinfo`/`squeue -u $USER`/`sacct`/`scontrol show job`.
- Home quota: 512 GiB (hard limit 2048 GiB, 14-day grace; `quota -s`). Keep home lean; big
  datasets/backups go under `/share/workspace2` (44 TiB) etc., not home. Do IO-heavy work
  (large copy/compress) on `storge`, not login01.
- A per-user CPU/QOS cap is in effect: when you submit many jobs, most sit
  `PD (QOSMaxCpuPerUserLimit)` and start as capacity frees. This is NORMAL, not an error.

## Submitting jobs

- Batch scripts live in `scripts/slurm/*.sbatch`. Run from the project root.
- Logs go to `logs/slurm/%x-%j.out` and `.err` (create `logs/slurm` first).
- Request only what you need (`--gres=gpu:1`, `-c`, `--mem`). Preprocessing / summarizers are
  CPU-only (no `--gres`).
- Activate inside the job (real base path on this cluster):
  ```bash
  source /share/software/anaconda3/2024.10/etc/profile.d/conda.sh
  conda activate mi_torch_cu118
  cd /share/home/yuan/SYX/eeg-mi-online
  ```
- **GPU jobs must fail-fast** if `torch.cuda.is_available()` is False (raise / exit non-zero;
  never silently train on CPU).
- Always smoke-test on a GPU node via `srun` (subjects 1,2, few epochs) BEFORE the full `sbatch`.
- Split big grids into many small jobs (e.g. method × model × seed) rather than one huge job;
  give each job collision-free output filenames; collect job ids to a file; submit the
  aggregation/summarizer as a dependent CPU job (`--dependency=afterany:<ids>`).
- Pass config paths as arguments. Useful: `sbatch --parsable`, `squeue -u $USER`, `scancel`,
  `sinfo`, `sacct -X -j <jobid> --format=JobID,JobName,State,Elapsed`.

## Storage / filesystem scope

- Code/configs/manifests/splits/outputs live under the project root
  `/share/home/yuan/SYX/eeg-mi-online`.
- The raw + processed dataset under `/share/workspace2/.../WBCIC_SHU` (path from
  `configs/paths.yaml`) is **READ-ONLY input**: read the `.npz`/manifest, but NEVER create,
  modify, or delete anything there.
- **Only write inside the project root.** Do not write outside `/share/home/yuan/SYX`, and do not
  write into sibling folders under `/share/home/yuan/SYX/` (e.g. senior handoff folders) — those
  are read-only references unless the user says otherwise.
